 "inputs": {
  "note": "deep-search runs its own release pipeline (bin/); this case replays the same sample against the kit's GKE window check, which every kit service runs. The service config is built for this replay: only the Deployment, its container and the image are deep-search's; tier check_rollback (no dev environment here) rolls back on its own like deep-search's full tier. The record keeps only the Deployment that failed (the other 23 workloads passed). Kubernetes events: the HPA set 15 replicas at 20:23:45 UTC; the last missing pod started at 20:24:43. The record keeps only the line '11/15 replicas available' of the 20:24:04 sample, so the sample is the deploy snapshot with those counts. No later sample was kept; replay sees this sample on every fresh read and does not invent a recovery. The failed release and its rollback target ran identical images.",
